# D-Bus session-bus activation file for jacket's notification daemon.
#
# Installed by packaging/install.sh into
#   ${XDG_DATA_HOME:-~/.local/share}/dbus-1/services/
#
# Why it exists: jacket IS org.freedesktop.Notifications. If the process
# crashes (or isn't running yet), senders' Notify() calls used to fail with
# "no such daemon" and the notification was lost forever. With this file the
# bus itself relaunches jacket on the next incoming Notify() — no lost window,
# no polling.
#
# While jacket owns the name this file is inert; activation fires only when
# nobody owns org.freedesktop.Notifications.
#
# NOTE: installing this makes jacket your notification daemon. If you'd rather
# use mako/dunst, don't install it (or remove the installed copy) — those
# daemons ship their own activation files.
[D-BUS Service]
Name=org.freedesktop.Notifications
Exec=jacket run
SystemdService=jacket.service
